# lsan-wayland.supp - the DOCUMENTED suppressions for the Wayland
# lane's two libwayland-client-internal allocations (CI catch,
# 2026-11-10; refined 2026-11-11).
#
# ROLE: documentation + a clang-LSan option file. CI consumes NEITHER:
# the shutdown-leak fixes (the five registry manager proxies, the
# test's discarded queue) made both sway targets leak-clean under
# plain detection, and gcc-14's libasan parser cannot consume
# suppression files reliably (the same valid file flips between
# parse-ok and a fatal parse-error). Leak detection stays fully ON in
# CI; this file names the two allocations so the pattern is on record
# for any run using clang's sanitizer runtime:
#   ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=1:suppressions=tests/lsan-wayland.supp
#
# WHY THESE TWO
#
# The Wayland client library's own allocations that survive
# wl_display_disconnect on libwayland-client 1.22 (ubuntu-24.04,
# debian stable): two 96-byte callocs whose stacks the unwinder
# cannot attribute past the ffi trampoline (the registry-global
# dispatcher). On the pinned 1.23 the same teardown is clean - the
# allocations do not exist.
#
# NARROWNESS
#
# LSan suppression entries match a symbol or a module name in the
# allocation's stack. Because the 1.22 stacks truncate INSIDE
# libwayland-client, the only honest frames are the library's own
# entry points named in the report:
#   - wl_proxy_marshal_array_flags (the wl_registry_bind path)
#   - wl_proxy_create_wrapper     (the queue wrapper path)
# A module-wide `leak:libwayland-client.so.0` would hide every future
# libwayland leak, so it is deliberately NOT used: these two entries
# name the two allocations' innermost FDK-independent frames and
# nothing else. Any NEW leak (FDK's or libwayland's) with a different
# shape still fails the suite.
#
# FDK's own proxy discipline is proven with detection ON:
#   - the X11 lane runs the same suite leak-clean,
#   - the five P3 create/destroy cycles run leak-clean on Wayland,
#   - the 2026-11-11 audit fixed the last real leaks (five registry
#     manager proxies in the connection shutdown, one discarded test
#     queue in test_matrix.c).
leak:wl_proxy_marshal_array_flags
leak:wl_proxy_create_wrapper
